==============================================================================
(3) THE VANISHING-SUMS BRIDGE (THM-415): why the saturation is trivial
==============================================================================
   CT(m) = sum over charge-reps of 0 of (multinomial) * (coeff monomial).  Setting all
   CT(m)=0 is a system of VANISHING SUMS of coefficient monomials.  THM-415: nontrivial
   vanishing needs 'composite' structure (a sublattice relation among charges).  The
   MINIMAL rep m0 is the primitive relation; its cancellation (CT(m0)=0) is ONE equation
   in the params, but CT(2m0) = (that)^2 + correction adds an INDEPENDENT equation, and
   the two generate the unit ideal after saturation -- exactly the trinomial gcd, now
   multivariate.  The 'correction' is the GMC-cascade surviving term (THM-1535).
